            "call_iLoPRQI5HgpHYGMYRAzfM1Dc__vscode-1782945660363": {
              "content": [
                {
                  "value": "\nusage: /Applications/Hammerspoon.app/Contents/Frameworks/hs/hs [arguments] [file\n]\n\n    -A         Auto launch Hammerspoon if it is not currently running.  The defa\nult behavior is to prompt the user for confirmation before launching.\n    -c cmd     Specifies a Hammerspoon command to execute. May be specified more\n than once and commands will be executed in the order they appear. Disables colo\nrized output unless -N is present. Disables interactive mode unless -i is presen\nt. If -i is present or if stdin is a pipe, these commands will be executed first\n.\n    -C         Enable print cloning from the Hammerspoon Console to this instanc\ne. Disables -P.\n    -h         Displays this help and exits.\n    -i         Enable interactive mode. Default unless -c argument is present, s\ntdin is a pipe, output is redirected, or if a file path is specified.\n    -m name    Specify the name of the remote port to connect to. Defaults to Ha\nmmerspoon.\n    -n         Disable colorized output. Automatic if stdin is a pipe, output is\n redirected, or if a file path is specified.\n    -N         Force colorized output even when it would normally not be enabled\n.\n    -P         Enable print mirroring from this instance to the Hammerspoon Cons\nole. Disables -C.\n    -q         Enable quiet mode.  In quiet mode, the only output to the instanc\ne will be errors and the final result of any command executed.\n    -s         Read stdin for the contents to execute and exit.  Included for ba\nckwards compatibility as this tool now detects when stdin is a pipe automaticall\ny. Disables colorized output unless -N is present. Disables interactive mode.\n    -t sec     Specifies the send and receive timeouts in seconds.  Defaults to\n4.000000 seconds.\n    --         Ignore all arguments following, allowing custom arguments to be p\nassed into the cli instance.\n    /path/file Specifies a file containing Hammerspoon code to load and execute.\n Must start with  ~, ./, or / and be a file readable by the user.  Disables colo\nrized output unless -N is present.  Disables interactive mode unless -i is prese\nnt. Like --, all arguments after this are passed in unparsed.\n\nWithin the instance, all arguments passed to the /Applications/Hammerspoon.app/C\nontents/Frameworks/hs/hs executable are available as strings in the `_cli._args`\n array.  If the -- argument or a file path is present, that argument and all arg\numents that follow will be available as strings in the `_cli.args` array; otherw\nise the `_cli.args` array will be a mirror of `_cli._args`.\n\nvitaliy@MacBook-Air-2 local-whisper % "
                }
              ]
            },
